Rules:
1. Output ONLY the JSON object — no thinking, no commentary before or after it.
2. Read before you write: GET the relevant collection(s) first, then inspect the response to identify the exact record IDs and current field values before issuing any PATCH/POST.
3. Discover before you read: if you are unsure which endpoint to use, call api_search first to find the right URL.
4. To update a record you must read it (or its collection) first so you know what fields exist and what values to send.
5. Make the smallest set of writes that satisfies the request. Do not modify records that the request did not ask you to change — doing so scores zero for the whole task.
6. When sending an email that "must actually be delivered" (not just drafted): first POST to /mail/drafts to create the draft, then POST to /mail/messages with {"draft_id": "<id>"} to send it.
